IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clpnt-dates`
IMPORT `clpnt-claims`

-- Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1994 (NT) -- worked cases for the questions of the person bringing a claim.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from an unofficial copy under
-- the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts and the answers used below`

`7 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 7 11 2026
`6 Nov 1994` MEANS `the calendar date` 6 11 1994
`7 Nov 1994` MEANS `the calendar date` 7 11 1994
`1 Jun 1993` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 1993
`1 Jun 1996` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 1996
`15 Feb 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 2 2020
`1 Mar 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2020
`10 Jun 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 6 2020
`28 Feb 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2023
`1 Mar 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2023
`2 Mar 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 3 2023
`29 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2024
`28 Feb 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2027
`1 Mar 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2027

`a State` MEANS `the law of an Australian State`
`another Territory` MEANS `the law of another Territory of the Commonwealth`
`NZ` MEANS `the law of New Zealand`
`NT law` MEANS `the law of the Northern Territory`
`a foreign country` MEANS `the law of a country other than Australia or New Zealand`
`NT court` MEANS `a court of the Northern Territory`
`NT arbitrator` MEANS `an arbitrator, in an arbitration held in the Northern Territory`
`outside NT` MEANS `a court or arbitrator outside the Northern Territory`

`APPLIES` MEANS `yes: the Act applies to these proceedings (s 3), even if the cause of action arose before 7 November 1994`
`TOO EARLY` MEANS `no: the proceedings were instituted before 7 November 1994 (s 3, the text's no)`

`THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW` MEANS `the limitation law of the place whose law governs the claim applies to it, as part of that place's substantive law (s 5)`
`S5 NOT UNDER THIS ACT` MEANS `not under this Act: it does not apply to these proceedings (s 3, the text's no)`
`S5 NOT AN NT COURT` MEANS `s 5 does not apply: the claim is not before a court or arbitrator of the Territory (the text's no: its "if" fails); this Act does not say which time limit applies`
`S5 NOT ANOTHER PLACE` MEANS `s 5 does not apply: the claim is not governed by the law of a State, another Territory or New Zealand (the text's no: its "if" fails); this Act does not say which time limit applies`

`IN TIME` MEANS `in time: you commenced on or before the last day the limitation law of the governing place allows (s 5)`
`STILL IN TIME` MEANS `still in time: you have not commenced, and the last day the limitation law of the governing place allows has not passed (s 5)`
`OUT OF TIME` MEANS `out of time under the limitation law of the governing place (s 5): only a discretion that law gives the court can help (see s 6)`
`NO TIME LIMIT FROM THIS ACT` MEANS `this Act does not make another place's time limit apply on these facts (s 3 or s 5, the text's no)`

`FAVOUR` MEANS `as the courts of that place do in comparable cases, and on these facts they would exercise it in your favour (s 6)`
`NOT FAVOUR` MEANS `as the courts of that place do in comparable cases, and on these facts they would not exercise it in your favour (s 6)`
`NOT PRACTICABLE` MEANS `s 6 asks the court to follow that place's courts only as far as practicable; here it is not practicable, and s 6 says no more (NOTHING-kind)`
`NO DISCRETION` MEANS `s 6 does not arise: that limitation law gives the court no discretion that you have asked it to exercise (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`S6 NOT NT OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE` MEANS `s 6 does not arise: not a court or arbitrator of the Territory, or not the limitation law of a State, another Territory or New Zealand (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`S6 NOT UNDER THIS ACT` MEANS `s 6 does not arise under this Act: it does not apply to these proceedings (s 3, the text's no)`

§ `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings`

-- Instituted on the commencement day itself: not "before that commencement", so the Act applies (edge).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` TRUE `7 Nov 1994` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `APPLIES`
-- Instituted the day before commencement (edge).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` TRUE `6 Nov 1994` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TOO EARLY`
-- Instituted in 1993.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` TRUE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TOO EARLY`
-- Instituted in 2020 on a cause of action of any age.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `APPLIES`
-- Not yet instituted: they will be instituted today or later; the date given is not used (fork F4).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `APPLIES`
-- Not yet instituted on a hypothetical "today" of 6 November 1994: instituting that day would be before commencement.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- does this Act apply to my proceedings` FALSE `7 Nov 2026` `6 Nov 1994` EQUALS `TOO EARLY`
#ASSERT `the Act applies` TRUE `7 Nov 1994` `7 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act applies` TRUE `6 Nov 1994` `7 Nov 2026`)

§ `s 4 -- is it a limitation law`

#ASSERT `s 4 -- is it a limitation law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4 -- is it a limitation law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4 -- is it a limitation law` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4 -- is it a limitation law` FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim`

-- Injury in a State, sued on in a Territory court: that State's limitation law.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
-- An arbitrator in the Territory counts as "court" (s 4; fork F2); New Zealand law governs; no proclamation needed.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `NT arbitrator` `NZ` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
-- Another Territory (fork F5).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `NT court` `another Territory` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
-- Not yet instituted.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `NT court` `a State` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
-- The Territory's own law governs: s 5's "if" fails.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `NT court` `NT law` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `S5 NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
-- A foreign country's law: s 5's "if" fails.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `NT court` `a foreign country` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `S5 NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
-- A court outside the Territory.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `outside NT` `a State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `S5 NOT AN NT COURT`
-- Forum is checked before the governing law.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `outside NT` `NT law` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `S5 NOT AN NT COURT`
-- Instituted before commencement: s 3 first.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `6 Nov 1994` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `S5 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `outside NT` `a foreign country` TRUE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `S5 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
-- Instituted on the commencement day (edge).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `7 Nov 1994` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`

§ `s 5 -- the regulative rule alone`

-- 1 March 2020 to 1 March 2023 is 1095 days (no 29 February in between).
#ASSERT `the days from` `1 Mar 2020` `to` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS 1095
#ASSERT `s 5 -- commencing on this day is in time` 1095 0
#ASSERT `s 5 -- commencing on this day is in time` 1095 1094
#ASSERT `s 5 -- commencing on this day is in time` 1095 1095
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5 -- commencing on this day is in time` 1095 1096)

§ `s 5 -- am I in time`

-- Three years running from 1 March 2020; last day 1 March 2023 (the governing law's last day, a fact).
-- Commenced on the last day (edge): in time.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `1 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- The day before the last day.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `28 Feb 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- The day after the last day (edge).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- On the day time began.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `1 Mar 2020` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- Before time began (fork F7: counted as day 0).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `15 Feb 2020` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- Not yet commenced; today is the last day (edge).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `a State` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `1 Mar 2023` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
-- Not yet commenced; today is the day after the last day (edge).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `a State` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `2 Mar 2023` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- Not yet commenced; last day still ahead.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `NZ` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` `29 Feb 2024` `1 Mar 2027` EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
-- A period running from 29 February 2024 with a last day of 28 February 2027 (that law's counting, a fact): on it, and the day after.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT arbitrator` `another Territory` TRUE `28 Feb 2027` `7 Nov 2026` `29 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2027` EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT arbitrator` `another Territory` TRUE `1 Mar 2027` `7 Nov 2026` `29 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2027` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- An arbitration in the Territory under New Zealand law, commenced on the last day.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT arbitrator` `NZ` TRUE `1 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- The Act does not make another place's time limit apply: Territory law, a court outside, a foreign law, too early.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `NT law` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM THIS ACT`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `outside NT` `a State` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM THIS ACT`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `a foreign country` TRUE `1 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM THIS ACT`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- am I in time` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `6 Nov 1994` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Jun 1993` `1 Jun 1996` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM THIS ACT`

§ `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law`

#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `FAVOUR`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT FAVOUR`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOT PRACTICABLE`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NO DISCRETION`
-- No discretion asked for is checked before practicability.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NO DISCRETION`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `NT arbitrator` `another Territory` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `FAVOUR`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `NT court` `NZ` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT FAVOUR`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `outside NT` `a State` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S6 NOT NT OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `NT court` `a foreign country` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S6 NOT NT OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `NT court` `NT law` TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S6 NOT NT OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `NT court` `a State` TRUE `6 Nov 1994` `7 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S6 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
-- s 3 is checked first.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `outside NT` `a foreign country` TRUE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S6 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
